      "claim": "When the bottle was sealed on the mountain top, the air inside was at the ambient pressure of that altitude.",
      "evidence": "The bottle was closed immediately after drinking, trapping the surrounding air without time for pressure equilibration.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "The valley, being at lower altitude, has a higher ambient pressure than the mountain top.",
      "evidence": "From step 1, pressure is inversely related to altitude; lower altitude → higher pressure.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": [1]
